# Title: Forfiles.EXE Child Process Masquerading
# ID: f53714ec-5077-420e-ad20-907ff9bb2958
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Anish Bogati
# Date: 2024-01-05
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036
# Description: Detects the execution of "forfiles" from a non-default location, in order to potentially spawn a custom "cmd.exe" from the current working directory.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((parent_process_exec="*.exe" OR parent_process_exec="*.exe\"") AND process_path="*\\cmd.exe" AND process_exec="/c echo \"*") AND NOT (((parent_process_path="*:\\Windows\\System32\\*" OR parent_process_path="*:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*") AND parent_process_path="*\\forfiles.exe" AND (process_path="*:\\Windows\\System32\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*") AND process_path="*\\cmd.exe")))
